# BUG-235 (NEGATIVE half) — this is the guard that matters.
#
# A bare `use` must NOT bind the dep's names. That is what QUICKSTART documents, and a
# period when it silently DID bind them is what rotted the Luau corpus: 1,780 translated
# scripts written against the lenient behaviour went from 1482 compiling to 849 when it
# was tightened, and nobody noticed for five weeks because nothing pinned the semantic.
#
# A positive test cannot catch a return to leniency — only this direction can. If this
# file ever compiles, `use` has started binding names again and the corpus rot is back.
use bug235_use_lib

def main()
    var a = Widget(7)
    print(a.value().toString())
